{"id":"8b9beb09-507a-4359-bc0c-8027737eece2","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-08-10T21:30:21.894Z","createdBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-10T21:30:21.894Z","lastModifiedBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 2","sequence":2,"activity":{"id":"1be7c542-b814-422c-8cfa-eb24a17c56dc","type":"activity","sequence":2,"group":{"id":"1be7c542-b814-422c-8cfa-eb24a17c56dc","type":"build","name":null,"sequence":5,"subgroups":[{"id":"1be7c542-b814-422c-8cfa-eb24a17c56dc","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"build 1","steps":[{"id":"49f342d0-eed1-437b-8b04-85b02781c49c","hints":"<p>❓ Did you click on the ⏷in the box to rename the sprite?</p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/k1az3nue.uuj.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Which block sets a sprite?&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you change the name from “mySprite” to something more descriptive?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Encourage the ninja to give sprites a simple yet descriptive name, as that will be helpful to refer to the sprite later on in the program.</p><p><br></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Add a </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> to this project, and select an image from the Gallery. This </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> will be the main character who is looking for their lost puppy.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Rename the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> with a simple, descriptive name such as “child”. Click the ⏷ in the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 0, 0); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[mySprite]</strong><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">name box</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">to open the drop down menu</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>, </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">then</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">select </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>Rename variable…</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Click ▶ to see the child </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> appear on the screen!</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"6b5dafff-9d44-42fd-891e-53b3c6f65a80","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you select the correct </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">name in the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(74, 134, 232); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set sprite position to]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/uz3ezpvl.wne.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Which block sets a sprite’s position?</p><p>❓Did you try out different x and y values to move the sprite’s position?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Remind ninjas that any block that refers to a <strong>sprite </strong>needs to come after its<strong> [set sprite to] </strong>block.</p>","instructions":"<p>Set the child <strong>sprite</strong>’s starting position. </p><p><br></p><p>Click the ⏷ on the<strong> (mySprite) </strong>bubble<strong><em> </em></strong>to open the drop down menu<strong><em>, </em></strong>then<strong><em> </em></strong>select the <strong>sprite</strong>’s name. </p><p><br></p><p>Then click in the white bubbles to change the <strong>x</strong> and <strong>y</strong> coordinate values.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the new position of the child <strong>sprite</strong>.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"20c5b020-674d-4ee9-8334-078dd8d8d6c9","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you type a message in the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[show long text]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> code block and change the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[bottom]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> value?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/wj5bfqto.ebx.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Did you drag the <strong>[show long text]</strong> block <em>inside</em> the <strong>[on start]</strong> block?</p><p>❓Did you try different positions for the dialog text box?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡Guide ninjas to update their sprite’s position if it is being blocked by the dialog text box.</p><p>💡 The splash screen is useful for the “title” of a project, whereas the dialog box (“long text”) can be used for directions. The say block is useful for sprite speech, but if the text is longer, consider using the dialog box so the text is easier to read.</p>","instructions":"<p>Add a text box to this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Game </strong>code block menu then drag a<strong> [show long text] </strong>block inside the<strong> [on start]</strong> container block.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Type “I’m looking for my puppy” in the text bubble. Click the ⏷ on the<strong> [bottom] </strong>value to open the drop down menu<strong><em>, </em></strong>then<strong><em> </em></strong>select a position for the dialog text box.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the dialog text box appear!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"86bf0806-6daf-4ea5-b1f2-b51cf91039ea","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set dialog frame to]</strong><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">block </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">on top</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> of the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[show long text]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/sheefzht.rv4.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Did you explore the dialog frame options and select one that you like?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Guide ninjas to see that they must set the dialog box frame before using the block that “shows” the dialog box on screen.</p><p><br></p>","instructions":"<p>Customize how the text box looks!&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Game </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [set dialog frame to] </strong>block on top of the <strong>[show long text] </strong>block.&nbsp;Click the gray square to select a frame from the Gallery.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the dialog box with a custom frame!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"a0aa9ffd-0ccc-4b63-bb19-b473f33521fb","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set dialog text color to]</strong><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&nbsp;block </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">on top </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">of the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[show long text]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/njo5x2ny.gty.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Where should the <strong>[set dialog text color to]</strong> block be placed?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Guide ninjas to see that they must set the dialog text color before using the block that “shows” the dialog box on screen.</p><p><br></p>","instructions":"<p>Switch up the dialog box text color! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Game </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [set dialog text color to] </strong>block on top of the <strong>[show long text] </strong>block. Click the gray bubble to select a text color.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the dialog box text in a different text color!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"ee3b1851-c84c-4ce5-a48f-09e79a3ae5ca","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you select the correct </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">name in the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(74, 134, 232); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set sprite position to]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/tkdij5gw.eaa.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Which block sets a sprite’s position?</p><p>❓Did you try out different x and y values to move your sprite’s position?</p><p>❓Which block creates a new dialog box?</p><p>❓Did you try different positions for the dialog box?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong></p><p>💡Encourage the ninja to look back at how they programmed their sprite’s position and the dialog box previously.</p><p>💡 The splash screen is useful for the “title” of a project, whereas the dialog box (“long text”) can be used for directions. The say block is useful for sprite speech, but if the text is longer, consider using the dialog box so the text is easier to read. </p>","instructions":"<p>Help the child <strong>sprite</strong> search for their lost puppy! </p><p><br></p><p>Set a different position for the child <strong>sprite</strong>, then use another dialog box to show that the child <strong>sprite</strong> still cannot find their lost puppy!</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see how the child <strong>sprite</strong> changes position when the new dialog box appears on screen.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"a1d0334e-e9fc-4599-a0af-592907dc2e93","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you add a new </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 0, 0); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set sprite to]</strong><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">and</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(74, 134, 232); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set sprite position to]</strong><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">block to the end of the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 255, 0); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> container?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/hch5bkut.idv.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:</p><p>❓Which block sets a sprite?&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>❓Which block sets a sprite’s position?</p><p>❓ Did you change the name from “mySprite” to something more descriptive?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Encourage the ninja to give sprites a simple yet descriptive name, as that will be helpful to refer to the sprite later on in the program.</p><p>💡 Remind ninjas that any block that refers to a <strong>sprite </strong>needs to come after its<strong> [set sprite to] </strong>block.</p>","instructions":"<p>The puppy has been found! </p><p><br></p><p>Make the puppy <strong>sprite</strong> appear by adding a second <strong>sprite</strong> to the project. Rename the sprite and set its position, too.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the puppy <strong>sprite</strong> appear on the screen!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"11158af3-61f0-4ad9-81f9-49baa4b46140","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you select the correct </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sprite </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">name in the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(74, 134, 232); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[set sprite position to]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ab3mrsad.kdd.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Did you select the main character sprite’s name in the <strong>[set sprite position to] </strong>block?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Guide the ninja to notice that the order of the code blocks matters.&nbsp;</p><p>💡Encourage the ninja to look back at how they programmed their sprite’s position and the dialog box previously.</p><p>💡 The splash screen is useful for the “title” of a project, whereas the dialog box (“long text”) can be used for directions. The say block is useful for sprite speech, but if the text is longer, consider using the dialog box so the text is easier to read.</p><p><br></p>","instructions":"<p>Move the child <strong>sprite</strong> to the puppy <strong>sprite</strong>! </p><p><br></p><p>Set a different position for the child <strong>sprite</strong> and use another dialog box to show that the child <strong>sprite</strong> has found their lost puppy!</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the child <strong>sprite </strong>find their lost puppy!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"eee49355-dfad-488e-9a45-638fdf408d88","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">💡 The </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">sequence </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">of the code blocks matters. Putting the blocks in a different order will change how the program runs.</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/fiwqukca.wh3.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Where did you place the background color and screen effect blocks? Do they work as you expected them to?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Guide the ninja to notice that the order of the code blocks matters.</p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">[play sound]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> block’s playback mode parameter should be left as </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">[until done]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> so the code that follows this block does not run until the sound has finished playing. Ninjas will explore other playback mode options in a later level.</span></p>","instructions":"<p>Add some creative details to the end of the story!&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Scene </strong>code block menu, drag a <strong>[set background color to] </strong>block and <strong>[start screen effect] </strong>block. Select a background color and screen effect!</p><p><br></p><p>Then, open the <strong>Music </strong>code block menu, drag out a <strong>[play sound] </strong>block and select a sound. Allow the sound to play <strong>[until done]</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see how the project looks with the ending.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"3d34ff06-23e4-4147-aef5-0ce730bb6891","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">❓ Did you add the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(153, 0, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[splash]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> code block to the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">top</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> of the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 255, 0); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"> container block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/vzidcqas.g4q.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓Where did you place the splash screen blocks? Does it work as you expected it to?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Guide the ninja to notice that the order of the code blocks matters.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>💡 The splash screen is useful for the “title” of a project, whereas the dialog box (“long text”) can be used for directions. The say block is useful for sprite speech, but if the text is longer, consider using the dialog box so the text is easier to read. </p><p><br></p>","instructions":"<p>Add a <strong>splash </strong>screen to the beginning of&nbsp;the project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Game </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [splash] </strong>block inside the <strong>&nbsp;[on start]</strong> container block at the top of the code.&nbsp;Click in the white bubble and type the name of the project.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the <strong>splash </strong>screen in action.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Where’s My Puppy?","project":{"editor":{"filters":[{"name":"sprites","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"spritescreate","active":true},{"name":"spritesetvel","active":true},{"name":"spritesetpos","active":true},{"name":"Sprite_blockCombine_set","active":true},{"name":"Sprite_blockCombine_get","active":true},{"name":"spriteFollowOtherSprite","active":true},{"name":"startEffectOnSprite","active":true},{"name":"spritedestroy2","active":true},{"name":"spritesaytext","active":true},{"name":"spritesetsetstayinscreen","active":true},{"name":"spritesetsetbounceonwall","active":true},{"name":"spritescreateprojectilefromsprite","active":true},{"name":"spritescreateprojectilefromside","active":true},{"name":"spritesoverlap","active":true},